// Aseprite/BYOND ICON_SUBTRACT approximation as a semi-transparent overlay
// using the layer's color: field as the darkening tint. World-background-
// independent, so it does not bleed onto the floor under the canister the
// way a canvas-kind subtract blend would.
//
// True subtractive blending (dst -= src) cannot be expressed in straight
// alpha-over compositing without canvas blend modes. The alpha-overlay
// approximation uses VtxModulate.rgb as the overlay color (a darker version
// of the band's c2, picked per gas in canister_layered_preview.yml) so the
// stripe keeps its hue while darkening, instead of going grey toward black.
//
// alpha = clamp(luma * 5.5, 0, 0.95) darkens proportional to the mask's
// luma — bright mask pixels (the strongest subtract spots) overlay the
// per-gas dark tint, dim mask pixels contribute partial darkening. The
// 0.95 cap keeps the brightest pixels just short of fully opaque so they
// don't paint over the underlying band entirely.

void fragment() {
    highp vec4 mask = zTexture(UV);
    highp float luma = dot(mask.rgb, vec3(0.299, 0.587, 0.114));
    highp float alpha = clamp(luma * 5.5, 0.0, 0.95) * mask.a;
    COLOR = vec4(VtxModulate.rgb, alpha);
}
